    {
      "q": "<p><span style=\"font-family: Cambria Math;\">13</span><span style=\"font-family: Cambria Math;\">.</span><span style=\"font-family: Cambria Math;\"> There are two symbols available for voters to cast their votes – Car and Umbrella. The </span><span style=\"font-family: Cambria Math;\">‘Umbrella’ got 2412 votes, which were 120% of the votes of the ‘Car’. How many votes </span><span style=\"font-family: Cambria Math;\">were</span><span style=\"font-family: Cambria Math;\"> cast in total?</span></p>",
      "o": [
        "<p>4400</p>",
        "<p>4500</p>",
        "<p>4200</p>",
        "<p>4422</p>"
      ],
      "a": 3,
      "s": "<p><span style=\"font-family: Cambria Math;\">13.(d)</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: Cambria Math;\">Given that Umbrella got 2412 votes</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: Cambria Math;\">Which is 120% of votes</span><span style=\"font-family: Cambria Math;\"> of Car</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: Cambria Math;\">So votes of car = <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>2412</mn><mn>120</mn></mfrac></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>×</mo><mo> </mo><mn>100</mn></math></span><span style=\"font-family: Cambria Math;\"> = 2010</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-family: Cambria Math;\">Hence total number of votes = 2412 + 2010 = 4422</span></p>"
    },
    {
      "q": "<p>7. <span style=\"font-family: Cambria Math;\">In a </span><span style=\"font-family: Cambria Math;\">panchayat</span><span style=\"font-family: Cambria Math;\"> election, there were two candidates A and B. Candidate A got 42% of the votes and lost t</span><span style=\"font-family: Cambria Math;\">o B by 8000 votes. What is the total number of votes?</span></p>",
      "o": [
        "<p>30,000</p>",
        "<p>50,000</p>",
        "<p>5,000</p>",
        "<p>3,000</p>"
      ],
      "a": 1,
      "s": "<p><span style=\"font-family: Cambria Math;\">7.(</span><span style=\"font-family: Cambria Math;\">b) </span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Difference between A and B’s votes = 58 </span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">-</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> 42= 16%</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">16% = 8000</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Total vote (100%) = 50000</span></p>"
    },
    {
      "q": "<p><span style=\"font-family: Cambria Math;\">13. The</span><span style=\"font-family: Cambria Math;\"> price of an article is first increased by 25% and later</span><span style=\"font-family: Cambria Math;\"> on, the price was decreased </span><span style=\"font-family: Cambria Math;\">by</span><span style=\"font-family: Cambria Math;\"> 30% due to a reduction in sales. Find the net percentage change in the final price of </span><span style=\"font-family: Cambria Math;\">the</span><span style=\"font-family: Cambria Math;\"> article.</span></p>",
      "o": [
        "<p>11.5% increased</p>",
        "<p>14% decreased</p>",
        "<p>13% increased</p>",
        "<p>12.5% decreased</p>"
      ],
      "a": 3,
      "s": "<p>13<span style=\"font-family: Cambria Math;\">.(d)</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Net percentage change in the final price of article = 25% - 30% - </span><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>25</mn><mo> </mo><mo>×</mo><mo> </mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><mn>100</mn></mfrac></math><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> = -5% - 7.5% = -12.5%</span></p>"
    },
